{
  "choices": [
    {
      "message": {
        "content": "{\n  \"source_routes\": [\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0301\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"An Exploratory Study for the Association of Gut Microbiome with Efficacy of Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor in Patients with Hepatocellular Carcinoma\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供肝细胞癌（HCC）背景下微生物组与 ICI 疗效无显著关联的阴性证据，指出肝硬化导致的背景菌群失调可能干扰常见预测标志物（如多样性）的普适性。用于 CH01 对比不同癌种间证据强度的异质性，并在 CH05 中作为“宿主病理状态特异性”限制预测模型泛化能力的典型案例，强调单一微生物特征无法跨越所有实体瘤类型。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0302\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Salivary microbiome changes distinguish response to chemoradiotherapy in patients with oral cancer\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"虽非 ICI 研究，但揭示了局部微生物组（唾液）通过调节宿主免疫蛋白（如 DMBT1）影响放化疗反应的机制类比。用于 CH03 拓展“非肠道微生物组介导免疫调节”的机制视野，提示黏膜免疫蛋白可能是连接微生物与治疗反应的潜在桥梁；在 CH05 中作为方法学警示，说明局部微环境微生物研究的复杂性及跨癌种/治疗模式外推的局限性。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0303\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"The Role of the Gut Microbiome in Cancer Immunotherapy: Current Knowledge and Future Directions\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"系统梳理了与 ICI 响应相关的特定菌属（如双歧杆菌、阿克曼氏菌）及代谢物（肌苷、SCFAs），并详述了 T 细胞激活、Treg 抑制等分子机制。用于 CH02 建立候选生物标志物列表，CH03 构建“菌群 - 代谢物 - 免疫”因果链条，CH04 评估 FMT 和饮食干预的临床前景，并在 CH05 中批判性讨论现有证据多为临床前模型推导及临床试验异质性的现状。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Impact of gut-microbiome altering drugs and fecal microbiota transplant on the efficacy and toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors: A systematic review\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"汇总了抗生素使用导致 ICI 疗效下降的大规模临床观察数据，以及 FMT 改善难治性患者预后的案例。提供了 FMT 起效的具体免疫机制线索（如增加 CD8+ T 细胞浸润、下调 IL-8）。用于 CH01 确立抗生素作为负面调节因子的临床地位，CH03 解释 FMT 重塑免疫微环境的生物学路径，CH04 评估微生物干预在克服耐药中的可行性及当前小样本研究的局限。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0305\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Modulating tumor immunity using advanced microbiome therapeutics producing an indole metabolite\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"展示了工程菌通过产生吲哚乙酸（IAA）激活 AhR 通路，上调 CXCL9/IFN-γ并抑制 IL-17A，从而增强抗肿瘤免疫的具体分子机制。用于 CH03 阐明“代谢物 - 受体 - 细胞因子”介导的免疫调节链条，特别是 AhR 通路在 T 细胞招募中的作用；在 CH04 中作为工程益生菌作为局部药物递送平台的技术可行性证据，探讨其在诱导长期免疫记忆方面的潜力。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0306\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Overcoming acquired resistance to cancer immune checkpoint therapy: potential strategies based on molecular mechanisms\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"阐述了肠道菌群失调介导 ICI 获得性耐药的机制，包括有益菌（如普拉梭菌）丰度与生存期的正相关，以及抗生素导致的菌群破坏与预后不良的关联。用于 CH01 支持菌群状态影响疗效的观点，CH03 描述菌群通过增强抗原呈递和 Th1 反应调节免疫的潜在路径，CH04 列举 FMT 和特定益生菌（如 EDP1503）作为克服耐药策略的早期临床证据。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0307\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"A yeast-based oral therapeutic delivers immune checkpoint inhibitors to reduce intestinal tumor burden\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"证明了工程化酵母口服递送微型抗体在 MSS 结直肠癌模型中降低肿瘤负荷的疗效，并伴随肠道菌群结构重排。用于 CH03 探讨局部递送形式对免疫微环境（如减少 Tregs）和共生菌群的潜在协同效应；在 CH04 中作为非细菌类递送载体（酵母）的安全性和药代动力学优势案例；在 CH05 中警示治疗本身引起的菌群变化不一定与疗效存在直接因果关系。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0308\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Gut microbiome for predicting immune checkpoint blockade-associated adverse events\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"开发了基于 14 种微生物特征的 irAEs 预测模型（RF14），并揭示甲萘醌（维生素 K2）生物合成增强可能通过抑制 NF-κB 通路降低毒性风险。用于 CH02 展示微生物组作为毒性预测生物标志物的具体面板，CH03 阐述维生素 K 类物质维持肠道免疫稳态的代谢机制，CH05 讨论平衡疗效与毒性的临床困境及代谢物补充作为选择性干预策略的潜力。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0309\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Immunomodulation by the Commensal Microbiome During Immune-Targeted Interventions: Focus on Cancer Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Therapy and Vaccination\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"总结了与 ICI 疗效正相关的特定菌群（如普拉梭菌、长双歧杆菌）及三大机制通路（SCFAs、MAMPs、细胞因子）。用于 CH02 确认高多样性和特定菌属的预测价值，CH03 构建树突状细胞成熟和 T 细胞极化的机制框架，CH04 对比疫苗与 ICI 中微生物调节的异同，为理解微生物组在免疫干预中的通用性与特异性提供背景。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0310\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Association of antibiotic exposure with overall survival and colitis in patients with stage III and IV melanoma receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors.\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH03\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供了黑色素瘤患者中近期抗生素使用与总生存期显著降低（HR 1.6-2.8）及严重结肠炎风险增加（HR 2.1）的强关联数据。用于 CH01 量化抗生素暴露对临床结局的负面影响，作为微生物组完整性必要的间接临床证据；在 CH03 中作为支持“菌群失调削弱免疫反应”假说的关键临床佐证，尽管缺乏直接微生物测序数据，但排除了重症感染本身的混杂影响。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0311\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Targeting the gut microbiota to enhance the antitumor efficacy and attenuate the toxicity of CAR-T cell therapy: a new hope?\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"虽聚焦 CAR-T，但揭示了微生物代谢物（如 SCFAs）通过增强 mTOR 活性和组蛋白去乙酰化抑制来重塑 T 细胞功能的机制，与 ICI 响应机制具有平行性。用于 CH03 提供代谢重编程增强效应 T 细胞的假设，支持“微生物 - 代谢物 -T 细胞”轴的普适性；在 CH05 中作为跨免疫治疗模态的比较视角，提示微生物调节策略可能适用于多种免疫疗法，但也需注意血液瘤与实体瘤的差异。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0312\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Biomarkers for immune-related adverse events in cancer patients treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"综述了 irAEs 预测生物标志物的现状，指出微生物组研究结果的不一致性和可重复性挑战，并对比了血液标志物与微生物标志物的优劣。用于 CH02 讨论微生物组作为预测因子的临床可行性和标准化难题，CH05 强调在缺乏统一标准下，微生物组标志物开发需面对与其他类型标志物（如细胞因子、基因型）竞争的现实，呼吁大规模前瞻性验证。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0313\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Impact of the microbiome on checkpoint inhibitor treatment in patients with non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"汇总了 NSCLC 和黑色素瘤中微生物组成分（如阿克曼氏菌、双歧杆菌）与疗效正相关的证据，并提出了 T 细胞归巢、分子模拟和代谢产物调节三大机制。用于 CH01 和 CH02 建立特定菌属与疗效的关联图谱，CH03 详述 CCR9/CXCR3 受体和细胞因子介导的远程调控路径，CH05 批判性分析观察性研究的局限性和不同技术平台导致的异质性。\"\n},\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0314\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The Association of the Microbiome with Melanoma Tumor Response to Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Treatment and Immune-Related Adverse Events (NCT05102773)\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n  \"CH01\",\n  \"CH02\",\n  \"CH03\"\n],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供了黑色素瘤患者中特定菌种（如产丁酸菌）与响应正相关，以及 Blautia luti 与“响应且无 irAE\"理想状态相关的实证数据。用于 CH01 和 CH02 细化响应者与毒性解耦的微生物特征，CH03 探讨 Lachnospiraceae 通过代谢和免疫调节发挥作用的潜在机制，支持微生物组可同时优化疗效和安全性的观点，尽管样本量较小且为观察性关联。\"\n    },\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0315\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Treatment outcomes and prognosis of immune checkpoint inhibitors therapy in patients with advanced thymic carcinoma: A multicentre retrospective study.\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供了胸腺癌这一罕见实体瘤中 ICI 疗效的基线数据，显示联合化疗优于单药，且未涉及微生物组分析。用于 CH05 作为对照情境，说明不同组织学亚型对 ICI 的反应存在固有差异，提示在寻找微生物组等精细分层因素前，必须考虑肿瘤本身的免疫原性差异，避免将非微生物因素导致的疗效差异误读为微生物调节失效。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0316\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"[Efficacy-enhancing and toxicity-reducing effects of TCM in immune checkpoint inhibitor-based anti-tumor therapy: a review of mechanisms and advances].\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提出中药通过恢复肠道菌群稳态增强 ICI 疗效并减轻毒性的概念框架，虽缺乏具体菌种数据，但确立了“菌群 - 免疫”作为中药起效的关键路径。用于 CH03 补充非西方医学视角下的微生物调节机制假设，CH04 将中药视为一种潜在的微生物组干预策略，探讨其在管理 irAEs（如结肠炎）中的临床应用潜力，尽管证据多为综述性且机制细节待验证。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0317\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"The gut microbiome and cancer response to immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"详细列举了多种细菌代谢物（如 GMDP、c-di-AMP、肌苷）通过特定受体（NOD2、STING、AhR）调节免疫的具体分子机制，并提供了 FMT 临床概念验证证据。用于 CH02 和 CH03 构建高分辨率的“菌群 - 代谢物 - 受体”机制网络，CH04 评估 FMT 的变异性及商业益生菌的潜在风险，CH05 强调从物种水平向功能基因水平研究转变的必要性。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0318\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Update on the prognostic value of a novel immune-related toxicity grading system (OST score) in patients with advanced solid tumours treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI).\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH03\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"建立了免疫相关毒性评分（OST）与生存获益的正相关关系，指出广泛的多器官免疫激活比单纯毒性严重程度更能预测疗效。用于 CH01 提供宿主免疫反应强度作为疗效代理指标的表型证据，CH03 支持“系统性免疫激活广度”是疗效关键驱动因素的机制假设，间接提示微生物组可能通过调节这种全身性免疫状态来影响 ICI 结局，尽管本研究未直接测量微生物组。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0319\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Interplay between Gut Microbiome, Metabolites, and Tumor Immunity: Mechanisms and Clinical Translation\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"全面综述了 SCFAs、胆汁酸、色氨酸衍生物等代谢物通过特定受体（GPR109A, AhR, A2AR）调节免疫细胞功能的分子机制，并总结了 FMT 和工程菌的临床转化进展。用于 CH02 和 CH03 提供详细的代谢物 - 受体 - 免疫细胞互作图谱，CH04 评估不同干预策略（益生菌、FMT、饮食）的临床证据等级，CH05 讨论代谢物双向效应及个体异质性带来的转化挑战。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0320\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"The dual role of the gut microbiota in breast cancer: from pathogenic mechanisms to emerging therapeutic\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"聚焦乳腺癌，提供了特定菌群（如阿克曼氏菌）和代谢物（如 IPA）通过维持 CD8+ T 细胞干性和调节表观遗传增强 ICI 疗效的机制证据，并提及 FMT 在克服耐药中的初步数据。用于 CH01 和 CH02 展示乳腺癌特有的微生物标志物，CH03 详述 IPA-Tcf7 超增强子轴等具体分子路径，CH04 探讨饮食模式（如生酮饮食）通过重塑菌群影响疗效的潜力，同时指出多数证据来自动物模型。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0321\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Effect of microbiome group on immune checkpoint inhibitors in treatment of gastrointestinal tumors.\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH04\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"概述了胃肠道肿瘤中微生物组调节 ICI 疗效的三大干预类别（益生菌、FMT、饮食），并指出益生菌可能改善治疗反应。用于 CH01 确立 GI 肿瘤中微生物组作为关键调节因子的背景，CH04 分类讨论不同干预策略的概念框架，尽管摘要缺乏具体机制细节和定量数据，但为综述提供了 GI 肿瘤特异性干预 landscape 的结构性素材。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0322\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"The gut microbiome, immune check point inhibition and immune-related adverse events in non-small cell lung cancer\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"全面汇总了 NSCLC 中抗生素暴露与预后不良的关联数据，以及特定菌种（如阿克曼氏菌）与疗效及毒性的关系。用于 CH01 量化抗生素风险，CH02 和 CH03 构建从微生物抗原呈递到 T 细胞活化的生物学路径，CH04 展望 FMT 和益生菌的临床前景，CH05 批判性讨论观察性研究的混杂偏倚及跨肿瘤类型比较的异质性。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0323\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"The dark matter in cancer immunology: beyond the visible– unveiling multiomics pathways to breakthrough therapies\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提出“癌症暗物质”概念，将微生物组纳入肿瘤微环境整体调控网络，强调多组学整合在解析微生物 - 宿主互作中的重要性。用于 CH03 提供超越单一菌群组成的系统生物学视角，解释微生物如何通过代谢和表观遗传修饰影响 TME；在 CH05 中作为方法论参考，倡导使用长读长测序和 AI 驱动的多组学分析来克服当前研究的局限性和不确定性。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0324\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Research progress on mechanisms of tumor immune microenvironment and gastrointestinal resistance to immunotherapy: mini review\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供了 GI 肿瘤中 FMT 联合抗 PD-1 再挑战实现~20% ORR 的临床证据，并指出乳酸杆菌丰度与更好预后相关。用于 CH01 展示微生物干预在难治性 GI 肿瘤中的具体疗效数据，CH03 和 CH04 强调除了菌群直接互作外，复杂的微环境（如 CAF、TAM）也是耐药关键，提示菌群调节需与其他微环境重塑策略结合，尽管机制细节多引用自其他研究。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0325\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Mechanisms of traditional Chinese medicine in enhancing the efficacy and reducing the toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors via regulation of the tumor microenvironment and gut microbiota\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"详述了特定中药成分（如葛根芩连汤、人参皂苷）通过富集双歧杆菌、乳酸杆菌等有益菌，增加 SCFAs 和色氨酸代谢物，进而激活 DC 和 CD8+ T 细胞的“菌群 - 代谢物 - 免疫”轴机制。用于 CH03 提供中药调节微生物组的具体分子路径，CH04 探讨中药作为微生物组调节辅助疗法的潜力，特别是在减轻 ICI 诱导的结肠炎方面，尽管多数证据来自临床前模型。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0326\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Microbiome-derived metabolome as a potential predictor of response to cancer immunotherapy\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提出了将微生物代谢产物（特别是 SCFAs）而非物种组成作为预测因子的观点，并展示了不同研究中 SCFA 水平与预后关系的矛盾结果（如抗 CTLA-4 中低丁酸预后更好）。用于 CH02 和 CH03 强调功能性代谢特征的重要性及情境依赖性，CH05 作为反例说明简单概括“SCFA 总是有益”的误区，提示需区分免疫检查点类型和肿瘤微环境状态对代谢物效应的影响。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Biomarkers of Immunotherapy Response in Patients with Non-Small-Cell Lung Cancer: Microbiota Composition, Short-Chain Fatty Acids, and Intestinal Permeability\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供了 NSCLC 患者中基线微生物组成、SCFAs 和肠道通透性与 ICI 反应无显著关联的阴性结果。用于 CH01 和 CH02 反驳“微生物普遍预测 ICI 疗效”的观点，强调在 NSCLC 中可能需要更复杂的模型或动态监测；在 CH05 中作为方法学局限的典型案例，说明标准化缺失和基线静态测量的不足可能导致假阴性，提示需考虑疾病特异性和时间动态变化。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0328\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Beyond the tumor: the role of the gut microbiome in triple-negative breast cancer\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"综述了 TNBC 中高微生物多样性和产 SCFA 菌群与更好疗效（PFS, pCR）的关联，并详述了 SCFA 增强 DC 成熟和 CD8+ T 细胞活化的机制。用于 CH01 和 CH02 建立 TNBC 特异性微生物标志物，CH03 阐述“肠 - 乳腺”轴及代谢物转运机制，CH04 讨论饮食和 FMT 干预的潜力，CH05 指出当前证据多为回顾性及动物模型推导，缺乏 TNBC 特异性 RCT 数据。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0329\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Abstract 2727: A designed live bacterial therapeutic restores responder-like microbiome profiles and improves immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) response in a predictive model.\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"展示了基于全谱微生物组构建 ICI 响应预测模型（AUC 0.62）及通过恢复“响应者样”菌群特征改善预后的计算生物学概念验证。用于 CH02 说明从单一生物标志物向综合预测模型转变的趋势，CH04 提出“微生物组重塑”作为克服无响应的策略，CH05 警示该研究仅为摘要级别且基于模拟，距离实际临床应用仍有距离，需区分预测性能提升与真实临床获益。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0330\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Digital immune twins and ai-integrated multi-omic biomarkers: Redefining personalized immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"详述了肠道微生物代谢物（SCFAs、肌苷）通过激活 GALT 中的 PRRs 促进 IL-12 和 I 型 IFN 产生，进而增强 CD8+ T 细胞活性的全身性调节路径，并提及“肠 - 肺轴”。用于 CH03 构建 NSCLC 背景下微生物介导全身免疫重塑的机制框架，CH05 探讨结合液体活检和 AI 多组学模型实时监测微生物状态的未來方向，尽管部分机制推导自其他肿瘤类型。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0331\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Antibiotic-induced loss of gut microbiome metabolic output correlates with clinical responses to CAR T-cell therapy.\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供了抗生素导致微生物代谢产物（SCFAs）丢失进而削弱 CAR-T 疗效的分子证据，揭示了“微生物代谢物 - 免疫细胞代谢适应性”机制。用于 CH03 类比说明微生物代谢物支持免疫细胞效能的普遍原则，尽管研究对象为 CAR-T 和血液瘤，但为 ICI 机制提供旁证；在 CH05 中强调跨治疗模态和肿瘤类型外推需谨慎，区分外源性细胞治疗与内源性免疫应答的差异。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0332\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"The metabolic dialogue between intratumoural microbes and cancer: implications for immunotherapy\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"聚焦肿瘤内微生物而非肠道微生物，详述了肿瘤内微生物代谢物（如乳酸、TMAO、肌苷）直接调节免疫细胞功能并增强 ICI 疗效的机制。用于 CH03 补充“非肠道来源”的局部代谢调控机制，区分肠道与肿瘤内微生物的作用路径；在 CH05 中作为概念澄清素材，强调微生物来源的空间异质性，避免将肿瘤内微生物的发现直接外推至肠道微生物组。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Navigating the gut–metabolite–immune axis: enhancing efficacy and mitigating toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"系统阐述了“肠 - 代谢物 - 免疫”轴，详细描述了特定菌群和代谢物通过 cGAS-STING、AhR 等通路调节 ICI 疗效和毒性的机制，并讨论了 FMT 和益生菌的转化障碍。用于 CH01-CH04 提供全面的机制解释和临床干预现状，CH05 批判性分析当前研究的方法学异质性、缺乏标准化协议及临床前与临床转化的鸿沟，强调情境依赖性。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0334\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Gut microbiome features associate with immune checkpoint inhibitor response in individuals with non-melanoma skin cancers: an exploratory study\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供了非黑色素瘤皮肤癌（NMSC）中微生物代谢功能的复杂发现：预测显示 SCFA 产生通路在非响应者中富集，且 L-精氨酸水平较高，与常见假设相悖。用于 CH01 和 CH02 展示不同肿瘤类型中微生物标志物的特异性及矛盾结果，CH03 和 CH05 作为反例说明代谢物效应的双向性和情境依赖性，提示简单的相关性不足以解释复杂的免疫微环境交互，需更大规模验证。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0335\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Neoadjuvant Immunotherapy and Intestinal Microbiota: Unraveling Their Roles in Anastomotic Leakage and Fistula after Colorectal Cancer Surgery\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"阐述了特定肠道细菌（如脆弱拟杆菌、双歧杆菌）通过调节 DC 功能和 T 细胞激活增强 ICI 疗效的机制，并讨论了 SCFAs 在维持肠道屏障和免疫平衡中的作用。用于 CH03 提供微生物介导 ICI 疗效增强的具体生物学途径，CH04 提出微生物组管理作为提高 ICI 疗效和管理术后并发症（如吻合口瘘）的潜在策略，尽管机制多基于理论推导和引用其他研究。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0336\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"The current status and prospects of gut microbiota combined with PD-1/PD-L1 inhibitors in the treatment of colorectal cancer: a review\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"列举了特定菌株（如 LGG, R. intestinalis）和 FMT 在 CRC 模型中通过 cGAS/STING、丁酸盐等机制增强 PD-1 抑制剂疗效的证据，特别关注 MSS 亚型。用于 CH01-CH04 提供 CRC 特异性微生物干预案例和详细分子机制，CH05 指出临床数据极其有限且多为动物模型推导，强调从单一菌株向合成生物学和生态工程转变的未来趋势及转化挑战。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0337\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Intratumoral Microorganisms in Tumors: Current Understanding and Emerging Therapeutic Strategies\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"综述了肠道链球菌富集与肿瘤内 CD8+ T 细胞浸润正相关，以及 SCFAs 和 TMAO 在不同肿瘤类型中调节 ICI 疗效的机制。用于 CH03 提供跨器官（肠道 - 肿瘤）互作的具体实例和代谢重编程机制，CH05 强调微生物调节活动的高度情境依赖性和肿瘤类型特异性，警示避免过度概括单一机制，并指出需进一步验证全身代谢影响和安全谱系。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0338\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"The role of the microbiome in immune checkpoint inhibitor colitis and hepatitis.\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提出了微生物组作为 ICI 诱导的结肠炎和肝炎潜在贡献者的概念框架，并暗示通过操纵微生物组管理毒性的可能性。用于 CH01 确立微生物组在 ICI 安全性管理中的重要地位，CH04 和 CH05 作为讨论副作用管理策略和未来研究方向的切入点，尽管摘要缺乏具体机制细节和实证数据，但提示了微生物组 - 免疫系统 - 药物毒性之间的可干预联系。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0339\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Association of proton pump inhibitor use with survival outcomes in cancer patients treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors: a systematic review and meta-analysis\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"荟萃分析证实 PPI 使用与 ICI 疗效负相关（HR>1），且仅在 ICI 前长期使用才显著，提示时间累积的菌群失调是中介因素。用于 CH01 提供药物干扰微生物组影响疗效的宏观流行病学证据，CH03 支持“菌群组成改变->免疫微环境改变->疗效下降”链条的临床合理性，CH05 强调严格管理共病用药（如 PPI）以优化 ICI 疗效的临床实践意义。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0340\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Immune checkpoint inhibitors and anti-vascular endothelial growth factor antibody/tyrosine kinase inhibitors with or without transarterial chemoembolization as first-line treatment for advanced hepatocellular carcinoma (CHANCE2201): a target trial emulation study\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供了 HCC 中 ICI 联合抗 VEGF 及 TACE 的真实世界疗效数据，指出高肿瘤负荷患者可能从联合局部治疗中获益更多。用于 CH01 展示除微生物外，肿瘤负荷和局部治疗等非微生物因素对 ICI 疗效的关键调节作用；在 CH05 中作为背景证据，说明在探讨微生物机制前需考虑宿主肿瘤生物学特征的复杂性，避免将非微生物因素导致的疗效差异误读。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0341\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Monitoring and Modulating Diet and Gut Microbes to Enhance Response and Reduce Toxicity to Cancer Treatment\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"综述了特定微生物特征（如 Ruminococcaceae, 阿克曼氏菌）与 ICI 疗效的关联，详述了代谢物介导的机制，并讨论了高纤维饮食和抗生素的影响。用于 CH01-CH04 提供全面的临床关联、机制假设和干预策略背景，CH05 批判性分析观察性研究的局限性和 conflicting results，强调饮食作为混杂因素的重要性及未来需要标准化协议和大规模 RCT。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0342\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"The Interplay Between the Gut Microbiome and Immunotherapy in Gastrointestinal Malignancies: Mechanisms, Clinical Implications, And Therapeutic Potential\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"聚焦 GI 恶性肿瘤，详述了抗原模拟、代谢物驱动（SCFAs, 胆汁酸）和髓系细胞调节等具体分子机制，并总结了 FMT 和抗生素管理的临床证据。用于 CH01-CH04 提供 GI 肿瘤特异性的机制解释和临床转化策略，CH05 指出多数强证据来自黑色素瘤，GI 癌中因果证明尚缺，强调需谨慎外推并关注 GI 特异性验证。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Integrative Oncology Approaches to Supporting Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Treatment of Solid Tumours\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"汇总了 FMT、活体生物疗法（LBTs）和高纤维饮食增强 ICI 疗效的临床证据，并阐述了 SCFAs 和特定菌株代谢物介导的免疫激活机制。用于 CH01-CH04 提供整合肿瘤学视角下的微生物干预策略和机制路径，CH05 强调益生菌效果的菌株特异性和矛盾性，指出需区分观察性关联与因果证据，并考虑整体生活方式因素的影响。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0344\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Role of immune checkpoint inhibitors in PDL1-negative, low TMB, stable MSI metastatic solid tumours: Single centre study.\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供了在缺乏主流生物标志物时，不同实体瘤部位对 ICI 疗效的巨大差异（头颈/肺 vs 胃肠/妇科），暗示肿瘤组织起源本身是决定疗效的关键因素。用于 CH01 和 CH05 作为反面案例或边界条件，说明即使没有特定微生物干预，某些肿瘤类型仍具免疫原性，而另一些则天然抵抗，提示在探讨微生物调节机制前必须考虑肿瘤本身的固有免疫特性。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0345\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"A Silent Saboteur of Immunotherapy: Antibiotic Use and Its Impact on Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors Efficacy, a Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis of Recent Studies\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"最新荟萃分析确认抗生素暴露与 ICI 疗效（OS/PFS）负相关（HR=1.16），特别是在 NSCLC 亚组，并阐述了菌群失调导致抗原呈递受损的机制。用于 CH01 提供负面调节因子的定量证据，CH03 解释从微生物群到免疫反应的潜在通路，CH05 强调抗生素管理的重要性，并指出空间微生物组差异（肠道 vs 瘤内）可能导致效应异质性。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0346\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Translating energy balance research from the bench to the clinic to the community: Parallel animal-human studies in cancer\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提出了“平行动物 - 人类研究”范式，确立肠道微生物群作为连接宿主可调节生活方式因素（饮食、运动）与 ICI 疗效的关键中介角色，强调 SCFAs 和肠道屏障功能的机制路径。用于 CH03 构建“宿主因素 - 微生物群 - 免疫治疗”的综合框架，CH05 指出微生物群受环境影响大（90%），提示生活方式干预的潜力，但需结合更详细实证研究验证因果机制。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0347\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Comedications with Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors: Involvement of the Microbiota, Impact on Efficacy and Practical Implications\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"综述了抗生素、PPIs、皮质类固醇等药物通过破坏微生物群平衡降低 ICI 疗效的证据，并强调了“初始免疫致敏”时间窗的重要性。用于 CH01 列举导致疗效下降的具体临床场景，CH03 解释药物干扰免疫激活窗口的时序依赖性机制，CH05 提出临床实践中需评估合并用药必要性的实际建议，尽管摘要缺乏具体微生物组成变化数据。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0348\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Role of Gut Microbiome in Oncogenesis and Oncotherapies\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"绘制了 7 种肠外癌和 6 种 GI 癌中微生物 taxa 与 ICI 疗效关联的图谱，区分了有益菌（如阿克曼氏菌）和致病菌（如具核梭杆菌）及其免疫调节机制。用于 CH01 和 CH02 提供跨癌种的比较视角，CH03 详述直接免疫调节和间接炎症/代谢效应机制，CH05 指出证据多来自观察性研究或小鼠模型，临床转化仍处于探索阶段，需谨慎外推。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0349\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Gut microbiome modulates response to anti–PD-1 immunotherapy in melanoma patients\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供了黑色素瘤中肠道微生物多样性及特定菌属（如普拉梭菌）与抗 PD-1 响应率及 PFS 的直接临床关联，并通过 FMT 实验暗示因果路径。用于 CH01 和 CH02 确立微生物组成分与治疗响应的统计关联，CH03 详述有益菌群促进抗原呈递和 CD8+ T 细胞活化的免疫机制，CH05 指出因果证据主要来自小鼠模型，人体应用需验证普适性。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0350\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Understanding How Pre- and Probiotics Affect the Gut Microbiome and Metabolic Health.\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"综述了益生元/益生菌调节肠道微生物群基础生物学背景及 SCFAs、TLR 介导的一般免疫机制，虽未涉及 ICI，但提供了理解微生物群系统性免疫调节环境的生理学依据。用于 CH03 作为机制部分的背景知识，说明微生物代谢物如何一般性地调节免疫通路，CH05 警示菌株特异性和研究变异性，强调不能将代谢健康领域的发现直接外推至 ICI 疗效预测。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0351\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Microbiome Modulation in Lung Cancer Immunotherapy: Unveiling the Role of Respiratory and Gut Microbiota in the PD-1/PD-L1 Response.\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"聚焦肺癌，列举了多种与 ICI 疗效正相关的肠道菌属（双歧杆菌、阿克曼氏菌等）及其临床证据，并详述了乳酸杆菌促进 DC 成熟、双歧杆菌模拟抗原表位等机制。用于 CH01-CH04 提供肺癌特异性微生物标志物、机制链条和干预策略（益生菌、FMT），CH05 指出部分机制基于动物模型，且不同菌株效果可能存在双面性，需考虑肿瘤微环境差异。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0352\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Lower respiratory tract microbiome dysbiosis impairs clinical responses to immune checkpoint blockade in advanced non‐small‐cell lung cancer\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供了下呼吸道微生物组独立于肠道调节 NSCLC 中 ICI 疗效的证据，鉴定出 Bacillus 为有益菌，Sphingomonas 为有害菌，并提出脂质/氨基酸代谢介导的局部免疫重塑机制。用于 CH01 和 CH02 支持位点特异性微生物组（肺 vs 肠）具有不同预测价值的观点，CH03 阐述局部微生物代谢影响免疫细胞浸润的具体机制，CH05 强调不能从单一研究推断肠 - 肺轴互作，需区分空间异质性。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0353\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Biomarkers predicting the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in hepatocellular carcinoma\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"综述了 HCC 中特定肠道菌群（如普雷沃氏菌、阿克曼氏菌）与 ICI 响应的关联，以及抗生素使用与预后不良的联系，并提出了胆汁酸介导和 T 细胞耗竭的机制假设。用于 CH01 和 CH02 提供 HCC 特异性微生物标志物和环境影响因素证据，CH03 阐述潜在机制路径，CH05 指出 HCC 中证据混合且多为观察性，因果关系未完全阐明，需谨慎外推至所有实体瘤。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0354\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"A uniform computational approach improved on existing pipelines to reveal microbiome biomarkers of non-response to immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"通过标准化重分析揭示了与 ICI 无响应（NR） consistently 相关的特定细菌物种（如 Veillonella parvula），并构建了基于 NR 物种的预测指数。用于 CH01 和 CH02 提供非响应者特异性微生物标志物列表，支持多物种指数优于单标志物的观点，CH05 批判性讨论方法学异质性对生物标志物发现的影响，指出抗生素暴露会降低预测准确性，强调标准化临床注释的重要性。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0355\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Clinical Evidence for Microbiome-Based Strategies in Cancer Immunotherapy: A State-of-the-Art Review\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"全面综述了微生物组特征与 ICI 结局的临床关联，比较了 FMT、饮食、抗生素等不同干预策略的效果，并详述了代谢物介导的机制。用于 CH01-CH04 提供跨癌种的临床证据汇总和干预效果定性比较，CH05 指出黑色素瘤数据过多而其他肿瘤证据不足，强调当前证据等级多为观察性或早期试验，需大规模 RCT 验证因果性。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0356\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Gut microbiome, a novel precision medicine biomarker for hepatocellular carcinoma\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"聚焦 HCC，详述了微生物组通过免疫调节、药物代谢和 TME 重塑三大机制影响 ICI 疗效，并提供了 FMT 和益生菌干预的现状。用于 CH01 和 CH02 提供 HCC 特异性临床证据，CH03 阐述肠 - 肝轴在其中的作用，CH04 讨论微生物靶向干预的潜力，CH05 指出 HCC 中直接因果证据较少，临床转化面临动态变化和缺乏标准化协议的挑战。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0357\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Leveraging beneficial microbiome-immune interactions via probiotic use in cancer immunotherapy\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"综述了益生菌在多种实体瘤中与 ICI 联用的临床观察结果，详述了 SCFAs、AhR、STING 等介导的免疫调节机制，并指出了商业混合益生菌的潜在无效性。用于 CH01-CH04 提供菌株特异性临床数据和详细分子机制路径，CH05 强调临床数据矛盾且不充分，多数机制源自小鼠模型，警示非标准化商业产品的风险及需区分菌株特异性。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"The role of gut microbiome in modulating response to immune checkpoint inhibitor therapy in cancer\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"总结了特定肠道微生物特征与 ICPI 响应率及生存结局的关联，详述了 T 细胞交叉反应、代谢物产生等潜在机制，并概述了 FMT 等干预策略。用于 CH01-CH04 提供基础资源和具体候选生物，CH05 指出关联多为观察性，机制多基于小鼠模型，强调不同癌种和地理区域的变异性，警示作者利益冲突可能影响结论客观性。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0359\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Gut microbiome on immune checkpoint inhibitor therapy and consequent immune-related colitis: a review\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"映射了肠道菌群与 ICI 疗效及结肠炎的双向关系，列举了有益菌和致病菌的具体例子，并讨论了 FMT 和益生菌缓解结肠炎的机制。用于 CH01-CH04 提供具体细菌名称和干预策略证据，CH05 指出预测结肠炎的微生物标志物不一致，机制多基于小鼠模型，强调缺乏大规模试验数据支持常规临床应用。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0360\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Adverse Effect of the Duration of Antibiotic Use Prior to Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors on the Overall Survival of Patients with Recurrent Gynecologic Malignancies\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供了妇科肿瘤中抗生素使用时长（≥14 天）与 ICI 总生存期降低的实证数据，支持抗生素诱导菌群失调削弱疗效的假设。用于 CH01 量化抗生素暴露对长期生存的具体影响，CH03 作为理论桥梁解释临床观察背后的生物学合理性，CH05 指出该关联为观察性且未直接测量微生物组，提示需考虑感染严重程度等混杂因素。\"\n}\n  ]\n}",
        "reasoning_content": "The user wants me to route a batch of 60 sources (P0301-P0360) to the 5 chapters of a shared outline for a review on \"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect?\"\n\nThe chapters are:\n- CH01: 临床证据格局：抗生素时机、FMT 试验与观察性数据 (Clinical evidence landscape: antibiotic timing, FMT trials, observational data)\n- CH02: 微生物特征：预测 ICI 反应的菌分类群与代谢物 (Microbial features: taxa and metabolites predicting ICI response)\n- CH03: 机制通路：免疫、代谢与屏障功能的分子中介 (Mechanistic pathways: molecular mediators of immunity, metabolism, barrier function)\n- CH04: 治疗干预：FMT、益生菌与饮食的临床可行性 (Therapeutic interventions: clinical feasibility of FMT, probiotics, diet)\n- CH05: 局限性、异质性与转化研究方向 (Limitations, heterogeneity, translational research directions)\n\nI need to read each source's B_review_planning and assign it to appropriate chapter(s) based on its actual content, research type, object, conditions, and depth. I should not just rely on broad claims but check what the paper actually provides.\n\nLet me go through each source:\n\nP0301: HCC study, exploratory, found no association between microbiome diversity and ICI efficacy in HCC. This is important negative/limiting evidence. Should go to CH01 (clinical evidence) and CH05 (limitations/heterogeneity).\n\nP0302: Salivary microbiome in oral cancer with chemoradiotherapy (not ICI). This is tangential - not directly about gut microbiome and ICI. Could be used for comparison in CH05 about non-gut microbiomes, but limited relevance. Might be CH05 for methodological comparison.\n\nP0303: 2023 review on gut microbiome in cancer immunotherapy. Comprehensive review covering taxa, mechanisms, interventions. Can be used across multiple chapters but primarily CH02 (taxa), CH03 (mechanisms), CH04 (interventions).\n\nP0304: 2022 systematic review on antibiotics and FMT impact on ICI. Directly relevant to CH01 (antibiotic evidence, FMT trials) and CH04 (FMT interventions).\n\nP0305: 2025 study on engineered bacteria producing IAA metabolite in CRC models. Mechanistic study. CH03 (mechanisms - metabolite-AhR pathway).\n\nP0306: 2023 review on overcoming ICI resistance. Covers microbiome as one mechanism. CH02 (taxa associated with response/resistance), CH03 (mechanisms), CH04 (intervention strategies).\n\nP0307: 2024 study on yeast-based oral therapeutic delivering checkpoint inhibitors. This is about engineered delivery, not gut microbiome modulation per se. Limited relevance to the core question. Could be CH04 for intervention strategies but note it's not microbiome modulation.\n\nP0308: 2024 study on gut microbiome predicting irAEs (toxicity), not efficacy. Relevant to CH02 (microbial features) but for toxicity not efficacy. Could be CH05 for limitations about efficacy vs toxicity distinction.\n\nP0309: 2021 review on immunomodulation by commensal microbiome during immune-targeted interventions. CH02 (taxa), CH03 (mechanisms - SCFAs, MAMPs).\n\nP0310: 2020 abstract on antibiotic exposure and survival/colitis in melanoma. CH01 (antibiotic clinical evidence).\n\nP0311: 2024 review on microbiome and CAR-T therapy. Not ICI-focused. Limited relevance. Could be CH05 for comparison across immunotherapy modalities.\n\nP0312: 2024 review on biomarkers for irAEs. Not primarily about microbiome. Limited relevance. CH05 for biomarker challenges.\n\nP0313: 2019 review on microbiome impact on ICI in NSCLC and melanoma. CH01 (clinical evidence), CH02 (taxa), CH03 (mechanisms).\n\nP0314: 2025 study on microbiome association with melanoma ICI response and irAEs. CH01 (clinical evidence), CH02 (specific taxa).\n\nP0315: 2022 abstract on ICI in thymic carcinoma. No microbiome data. Not relevant for this review's core question. CH05 only as contrast for tumor heterogeneity.\n\nP0316: 2026 review on TCM and ICI. Mentions microbiome restoration as one mechanism. CH04 (intervention strategies - TCM), CH03 (mechanisms).\n\nP0317: 2025 review on gut microbiome and cancer response to ICI. Comprehensive. CH02 (taxa), CH03 (mechanisms - metabolites), CH04 (FMT, interventions).\n\nP0318: 2024 abstract on OST toxicity grading and prognosis. No microbiome data. Limited relevance. CH05 for toxicity-efficacy relationship context.\n\nP0319: 2026 review on microbiome, metabolites, tumor immunity. CH02 (metabolites), CH03 (mechanisms), CH04 (interventions).\n\nP0320: 2025 review on gut microbiota in breast cancer. CH02 (taxa in BC), CH03 (mechanisms - IPA, SCFAs), CH04 (FMT, diet).\n\nP0321: 2023 abstract on microbiome and ICI in GI tumors. CH01 (clinical evidence in GI), CH04 (interventions).\n\nP0322: 2022 review on gut microbiome, ICI and irAEs in NSCLC. CH01 (antibiotic evidence), CH02 (taxa in NSCLC), CH03 (mechanisms).\n\nP0323: 2025 review on multiomics in cancer immunology. Mentions microbiome as part of \"dark matter\". CH03 (mechanisms - conceptual), CH05 (methodological considerations).\n\nP0324: 2025 mini-review on GI tumor immune microenvironment and resistance. CH01 (FMT clinical evidence in GI), CH03 (mechanisms - TIME).\n\nP0325: 2026 review on TCM mechanisms via microbiome and TME. CH03 (mechanisms - TCM-microbiome-immune axis), CH04 (TCM interventions).\n\nP0326: 2020 paper on microbiome-derived metabolome as predictor. CH02 (metabolites as biomarkers), CH03 (mechanisms - SCFAs).\n\nP0327: 2024 study on NSCLC - negative findings for microbiome predicting ICI response. CH01 (clinical evidence - negative), CH05 (limitations, heterogeneity).\n\nP0328: 2026 review on gut microbiome in TNBC. CH02 (taxa in BC), CH03 (mechanisms - SCFAs, LPS), CH04 (interventions).\n\nP0329: 2026 abstract on designed bacterial therapeutic. CH04 (intervention strategies - engineered bacteria).\n\nP0330: 2026 review on digital immune twins and multi-omic biomarkers in NSCLC. CH03 (mechanisms - gut-lung axis), CH05 (methodological - AI integration).\n\nP0331: 2024 abstract on antibiotic-induced loss of microbiome metabolic output and CAR-T response. CH03 (mechanisms - SCFAs and immune cell function), CH01 (antibiotic impact).\n\nP0332: 2025 review on intratumoural microbes and cancer metabolism. CH03 (mechanisms - intratumoural vs gut), CH05 (conceptual distinctions).\n\nP0333: 2026 review on gut-metabolite-immune axis for ICI. CH02 (metabolites), CH03 (mechanisms), CH04 (interventions).\n\nP0334: 2025 study on non-melanoma skin cancers and microbiome. CH02 (taxa in NMSC), CH05 (heterogeneity across tumor types).\n\nP0335: 2024 review on neoadjuvant immunotherapy and intestinal microbiota in CRC surgery. CH03 (mechanisms - SCFAs, immune modulation), CH04 (interventions).\n\nP0336: 2025 review on gut microbiota + PD-1/PD-L1 in CRC. CH02 (specific strains in CRC), CH03 (mechanisms - cGAS/STING, butyrate), CH04 (interventions).\n\nP0337",
